{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema","id":649014,"title":"Why would a DB of the Realm join a group of Anathema?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T09:03:58-07:00","id":649014,"title":"Why would a DB of the Realm join a group of Anathema?","content":"I have been bored recently and brainstormed a circle for a comedy Exalted fic/story/<i>something</i> that I will probably never write. The first two members I came up with were a Solar and a Lunar, of course, so I <i>had</i> to have a DB in there.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I love Exalted and read the books, but I have immense trouble finding a game. I have been in exactly <i>one</i> Exalted session (not game, <i>session--</i>indeed it was the <i>only RPG session I have ever been in</i>) in my entire life back when I was as a freshman in high school (I'm a college sophomore now), in a game that ended in two sessions due to a legit pedo in our group (long story). As such, I have a semi-decent grasp of Exalted canon, but I have basically seen zero actual Exalted in action. So I'm not sure how people do this. I came up with a few ideas, but they feel unsatisfactory:<br /> <br /> 1: The Dynast becomes disillusioned with the Realm. This doesn't seem like a plausible idea, though. The Realm goes to literally every length possible to exult DB's as bodhisattvas who are literally incapable of doing wrong. I can understand a Realm citizen who's used to getting fucked becoming disillusioned, but Dynasts get basically everything. Why rebel against a system where you are at the absolute top, no questions asked?<br /> <br /> 2: The Dynast realizes the lies and truth the Realm spreads, discovering the actual history of Creation. Now...how is he to do this? The Realm censors everything heavily and even the goddamn historians and sorcerers themselves are pretty in the dark. How did this random Fire-Aspect learn about the Usurpation and the First Age, etc?<br /> <br /> 3: He sees the &quot;Anathema&quot; do some glorious things and decides to follow them, confused or interested. However the Immaculate Philosophy's indoctrination is so deep and strong that he would probably rationalize it away. This is what happened to Ten Winds in Keychain of Creation, but he was an old monk who had seen this happen over and over again. The Fire-Aspect we're talking about here Exalted at 15-or-so less than a decade before he joins the circle.<br /> <br /> 4: He's really fucking bored and just joins them 'cause why the fuck not<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering why he would do this. What would drive a DB to join this Solar and Lunar? I don't want to use Solar brainwash bullshit or Lunar deception, I want this choice to be his own. Sorry if this has been discussed endlessly on the forum and I'm just wasting space.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe I am vastly overthinking a story where a major character is a Sidereal who owns a Starmetal kazoo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:07:16-07:00","id":649041,"title":"","content":"Well does your DB have to be a Dynast? Can't they be an Outcaste from a culture that isn't as into the Immaculate faith, or doesn't believe it at all?<br /> <br /> (Also keep in mind, Ten Winds' initial backstory wasn't a lie, but it was incomplete: he had an additional and much more compelling reason for joining the circle, spoilers if you haven't read the whole comic.)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ten Winds wanted to retire from the All-Seeing Eye, which is hard when they're super-spy Exalted with Sidereals among them, and retirement isn't allowed. So he picked allies who could not possibly be allied with the Eye. And as a member of the Eye's super-secret inner group, he had already been told the truth about Celestial Exalted, so the only question was whether these particular Celestials would do something to his or the Realm's detriment.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> That said, Ten Winds' and Misho's weird backstories are elaborate excuses to put a ridiculously powerful elder Immaculate and a literal First Age Solar in the same group in a comedy story.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, it's plausible for an intelligent and curious Dynast to learn some of the truth. Some of them do know at least about Sidereals, and their religion contains so many lies (and probably contradictions) that at least some Dynasts must notice it doesn't add up. It's also plausible for a Dynast with a strong conscience to have doubts about how the Realm oppresses people, or even about the Wyld Hunt -- look at Cynis Avaku.<br /> <br /> But such characters are still Dynasts. They have a good life -- why would they throw away privilege, wealth, and power unparallelled in Creation? Why would they abandon their entire society and family? Suspecting or believing that there are lies or even moral problems in the Realm isn't enough reason for them to leave. Just uncovering the truth about the Celestials and the Usurpation doesn't necessarily motivate a Dynast to care that they're oppressing innocent Celestials, because the Dynasty are benefitting from it and what's the alternative, really? Those Celestials would challenge their empire and take away their wealth, if they let them live. The Realm can't survive if Lunars and Solars are able to consolidate their own kingdoms. Murdering Celestial Exalted won't look like a moral problem to a Dynast who's happy to hurt and kill mortals for their House's gain.<br /> <br /> In real life, people who disagree with or oppose their own society or government sometimes move away, or rebel, but plenty stick around because they still have strong ties to the place and maybe hope they can change some things.<br /> <br /> Things might be different if it becomes personal. You're a Dynast, perhaps a low-ranked one who has experienced just enough sneering from the higher-up to have some sympathy for those less fortunate than you*. You have a mortal relative -- a sibling, nephew, aunt, uncle, maybe even your spouse or kid or parent -- who exalts as a Lunar or Solar. You weren't dedicated enough to the faith to just kill them or take them to the monks -- for whatever reason you don't feel entirely <i><b>certain</b></i> that a demonic parasite has murdered your loved one and hijacked their body. Emotionally or even intellectually, you hope/doubt/fear that they might still be <i><b>them</b></i>. What do you do? Maybe you help them run away, but get caught. Then you're on the run, too. You didn't want to leave the Realm, but you can't go back now. With your relative (or not, if they were killed or separated from you) you have to escape to the Threshold if you want to live. You might still support the Realm as a civilization, while becoming uncomfortable with or downright opposed to the Wyld Hunt. (Iselsi Shen is a Solar and he still supports the All-Seeing Eye for I-can't-imagine-what-reason.)<br /> <br /> *I don't think it's a coincidence that Avaku was given a background as the sole Exalt of a trashy, despised bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-02-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:10:01-07:00","id":649046,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0004.html\" target=\"_blank\">Keychain of the Creation</a> had a former Immaculate Monk Join the a group of Anathema. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:13:48-07:00","id":649048,"title":"","content":"I ran a game recently where events conspired to have an Immaculate monk team up with a Solar circle, both for self-preservation and to combat a worse threat. The dynamic of mutual mistrust was quite entertaining.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649046#post649046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0004.html\" target=\"_blank\">Keychain of the Creation</a> had a former Immaculate Monk Join the a group of Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>KoC is fun but like a lot of stories it misses the core of the Immaculate teachings. The idea is not that the Anathema are absolute monsters all the time, it's that by taking power beyond their station and transgressing outside the coils of enlightenment, <i>anything </i>they do contributes to spiritual decay in themselves and others. Whether they actually act evil or not is immaterial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 09-02-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:30:15-07:00","id":649057,"title":"","content":"There's a goal that requires their mutual resources in the short term. Characters may or may not be overt about the idea that once that is fulfilled, all future interactions will revert, if not outright declaring &quot;once we've accomplished this, I'm going to try and kill you&quot;. Characters might develop towards revising this idea, especially in the form of continuously delaying it rather than outright disavowing it. There's always some other thing to go after that warrents keeping them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:51:31-07:00","id":649069,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel better, not too long ago I read a story by a somewhat popular author about a Solar who got a DB magistrate to join his rebellion against the Realm by kicking the crap out of her. Kind of like a pokemon. So whatever you come up with it'll probably be better than that.<br /> <br /> Something that might work is having the Realm screw them over somehow. True they're the 1% of the empire, but even Dynasts are scapegoats sometimes. You could have him know a lot about the immaculate lies, then have him take the fall for something he didn't do, and when he gets fed up with all the crap, possibly because of an attempted assassination, that's when he decides to maybe see what the whole anathema thing is really about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:56:37-07:00","id":649073,"title":"","content":"There are people living in stations of high privilege IRL who reject the system that privileges them as inherently unequal and terrible. <br /> <br /> While it's harder and less likely for that to occur in a setting with an aristocratic class and less ability to expose yourself to the inequity that you don't really see because it doesn't personally affect you, it's by no means impossible. <br /> <br /> Take a page from the book of Gautama. Hell, take a page from Mahasamatman in Lord of Light. You can live in pleasure and relative ignorance and have your opinions turned quite hardline against the system when you actually see the conditions of the oppressed or bad things happen to the people you care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:59:53-07:00","id":649089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649048#post649048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KoC is fun but like a lot of stories it misses the core of the Immaculate teachings. The idea is not that the Anathema are absolute monsters all the time, it's that by taking power beyond their station and transgressing outside the coils of enlightenment, <i>anything </i>they do contributes to spiritual decay in themselves and others. Whether they actually act evil or not is immaterial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what we later learn about Ten Winds it's likely he's more in the know about things than he was letting on at the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:03:25-07:00","id":649093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649041#post649041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well does your DB have to be a Dynast? Can't they be an Outcaste from a culture that isn't as into the Immaculate faith, or doesn't believe it at all?<br /> <br /> (Also keep in mind, Ten Winds' initial backstory wasn't a lie, but it was incomplete: he had an additional and much more compelling reason for joining the circle, spoilers if you haven't read the whole comic.)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ten Winds wanted to retire from the All-Seeing Eye, which is hard when they're super-spy Exalted with Sidereals among them, and retirement isn't allowed. So he picked allies who could not possibly be allied with the Eye. And as a member of the Eye's super-secret inner group, he had already been told the truth about Celestial Exalted, so the only question was whether these particular Celestials would do something to his or the Realm's detriment.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> That said, Ten Winds' and Misho's weird backstories are elaborate excuses to put a ridiculously powerful elder Immaculate and a literal First Age Solar in the same group in a comedy story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want a Dynast because I like the idea of one rebelling and want a character who knows the Realm. On the other hand, the Solar of the circle was a Dynast himself who never Exalted as a DB but later become a Solar; maybe there doesn't have to be two former-Dynasts in the same group.<br /> <br /> And yeah I read KoC, I really hope the author manages to get better and continue it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things might be different if it becomes personal. You're a Dynast, perhaps a low-ranked one who has experienced just enough sneering from the higher-up to have some sympathy for those less fortunate than you*. You have a mortal relative -- a sibling, nephew, aunt, uncle, maybe even your spouse or kid or parent -- who exalts as a Lunar or Solar. You weren't dedicated enough to the faith to just kill them or take them to the monks -- for whatever reason you don't feel entirely <i><b>certain</b></i> that a demonic parasite has murdered your loved one and hijacked their body. Emotionally or even intellectually, you hope/doubt/fear that they might still be <i><b>them</b></i>. What do you do? Maybe you help them run away, but get caught. Then you're on the run, too. You didn't want to leave the Realm, but you can't go back now. With your relative (or not, if they were killed or separated from you) you have to escape to the Threshold if you want to live. You might still support the Realm as a civilization, while becoming uncomfortable with or downright opposed to the Wyld Hunt. (Iselsi Shen is a Solar and he still supports the All-Seeing Eye for I-can't-imagine-what-reason.) </div> </div> </div>Hmm...maybe I can link together this guy and the Solar. Maybe they were part of the same house so the DB isn't immediately going to go into &quot;ANATHEMA FUCKING DIIIIE&quot; mode.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649057#post649057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a goal that requires their mutual resources in the short term. Characters may or may not be overt about the idea that once that is fulfilled, all future interactions will revert, if not outright declaring &quot;once we've accomplished this, I'm going to try and kill you&quot;. Characters might develop towards revising this idea, especially in the form of continuously delaying it rather than outright disavowing it. There's always some other thing to go after that warrents keeping them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I don't want that. I want him to join of his own free will, not just to get some shit done and then break ways. This is a comedy story at heart, though not a gag comedy. Think...Gintama, maybe? There's a lot of humor but it's not just a bunch of disconnected skits, there's still an actual plot. I want a logical reason for him to join but this isn't a super-serious hard look at the Realm and what it does to people.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is a story where a major character is a Twilight who built an Orichalcum clothes iron called &quot;THE WRINKLEFUCKER&quot; (all-caps mandatory by the way, and yes that is a reference to MSPA), which is pretty much a useless piece of shit since it weighs as much as a house and the essence-powered steam vent system tends to be more &quot;essence-powered flamethrower of scalding death&quot; so...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-02-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:19:33-07:00","id":649097,"title":"","content":"Well, given that, you can give the DB a silly reason for leaving the Realm, instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:23:59-07:00","id":649098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649097#post649097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, given that, you can give the DB a silly reason for leaving the Realm, instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but I want to maintain a sense of seriousness. It's hard to describe.<br /> <br /> Homestuck might actually be a good example of what I mean. It's a completely serious story, but it's filled with absurd references and humorous happenings in the middle of the actual plot. I hope I don't sound too flippant or like a dick, sorry if I do.<br /> <br /> Likewise for this story: yes, there's a Twilight sorceress who built an orichalcum clothes iron called &quot;THE WRINKLEFUCKER&quot;, and yes there's a Sidereal who owns a Starmetal kazoo that is just a wire-outline of a kazoo making it damn near useless, and yes the Solar leading the group is an absurdly passionate wrecking ball...but it's still an Exalted story about a circle who goes around doing grand shit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 09-02-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:25:37-07:00","id":649099,"title":"","content":"Or they could just be related. KoC gave us &quot;it's one thing to hear about the evils of anathema, and another to look your sibling in the eye and see nothing has changed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Having several siblings, one of whom I'm not all that friendly with, I can attest to the power of having grown together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","user":"Owill0w","date":". 09-02-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","name":"Owill0w","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:41:51-07:00","id":649115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Owill0w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649099#post649099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could just be related. KoC gave us &quot;it's one thing to hear about the evils of anathema, and another to look your sibling in the eye and see nothing has changed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Having several siblings, one of whom I'm not all that friendly with, I can attest to the power of having grown together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is pretty much the reason why my Twilight's Water Aspect brother is an ally on her character sheet instead of hunting her down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there are a lot of instances in real life where Americans go and reject the Western Lifestyle. Some join the Peace Corps. Others join Al-Qaeda. Or go the Martin Luther route of &quot;The Immaculate Religion is a Lie!&quot; and have to leave before the Wyld Hunt goes after you as a Heretic. Or Edward Snowden route of finding out that there are &quot;Anathema*&quot; running the Scarlet Empire behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> *Depending on your character's definition of Anathema includes Sidereals or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-02-2015, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:31:46-07:00","id":649145,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Erinys;n649041]why would they throw away privilege, wealth, and power unparallelled in Creation?QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yeah, about that...the jade is running out. I can think of several fictional DB-analogues who'd ditch the old system once it stopped giving them, say, free champagne. Cutbacks are never popular.<br /> <br /> ...Wasn't there a guy in <i>Pirates of the Caribbean</i> who literally gave up his old life to become Charon- and thereby get more rum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 09-02-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:57:45-07:00","id":649156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I want him to join of his own free will, not just to get some shit done and then break ways.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ruthless pragmatism doesn't come from free will? Regardless: &quot;Good night, Anathema. Good work. Sleep well. I'll most likely kill you in the morning.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:02:39-07:00","id":649159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649156#post649156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ruthless pragmatism doesn't come from free will? Regardless: &quot;Good night, Anathema. Good work. Sleep well. I'll most likely kill you in the morning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I worded that badly, what I meant is that he joins them because he earnestly wants to travel and do stuff with them, not to achieve some goal and then kick them to the curb.<br /> <br /> Of course, I could go the route you suggest, and then have their actions convince him that maybe the Anathema aren't the twisted demons he thought they were. Also looking back at it, &quot;two characters who hate each other have to work together&quot; is <i>perfect</i> for comedic shenanigans and all-round wackiness. This might work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:15:04-07:00","id":649163,"title":"","content":"I'm going to try and go for a neutral tone of developing a concept rather than hammering down on somebody for &quot;being wrong&quot;, so if you feel I'm doing the latter, please tell me so that I can adjust or cease. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he joins them because he earnestly wants to travel and do stuff with them, not to achieve some goal and then kick them to the curb.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suppose that for something like that, it depends on how passionate one imagines a Dragon Blood needs to be about this whole Wyld Hunt thing. I mean, sure, the majority of them are because they're conditioned and empowered to be, but I could see a character who would approach the whole thing in a dispassionate manner based on a perceived obligation that they don't strictly see as being an obstacle to doing stuff with those Exalted. That plus the idea of people who can have relationships in which the possibility that they'll need to have a fight that will end in at least one death one day in a manner that lacks malice or distrust, especially if they're of a type who approaches being a warrior as a kind of sport. One doesn't even have to look on still existing dangerous sports for that kind of mindset, since it was present in the earlier forms of tourney and a fair few dueling cultures. People can be a bit devil-may-care about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:39:11-07:00","id":649194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema#post649014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been bored recently and brainstormed a circle for a comedy Exalted fic/story/<i>something</i> that I will probably never write. The first two members I came up with were a Solar and a Lunar, of course, so I <i>had</i> to have a DB in there.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I love Exalted and read the books, but I have immense trouble finding a game. I have been in exactly <i>one</i> Exalted session (not game, <i>session--</i>indeed it was the <i>only RPG session I have ever been in</i>) in my entire life back when I was as a freshman in high school (I'm a college sophomore now), in a game that ended in two sessions due to a legit pedo in our group (long story). As such, I have a semi-decent grasp of Exalted canon, but I have basically seen zero actual Exalted in action. So I'm not sure how people do this. I came up with a few ideas, but they feel unsatisfactory:<br /> <br /> 1: The Dynast becomes disillusioned with the Realm. This doesn't seem like a plausible idea, though. The Realm goes to literally every length possible to exult DB's as bodhisattvas who are literally incapable of doing wrong. I can understand a Realm citizen who's used to getting fucked becoming disillusioned, but Dynasts get basically everything. Why rebel against a system where you are at the absolute top, no questions asked?<br /> <br /> 2: The Dynast realizes the lies and truth the Realm spreads, discovering the actual history of Creation. Now...how is he to do this? The Realm censors everything heavily and even the goddamn historians and sorcerers themselves are pretty in the dark. How did this random Fire-Aspect learn about the Usurpation and the First Age, etc?<br /> <br /> 3: He sees the &quot;Anathema&quot; do some glorious things and decides to follow them, confused or interested. However the Immaculate Philosophy's indoctrination is so deep and strong that he would probably rationalize it away. This is what happened to Ten Winds in Keychain of Creation, but he was an old monk who had seen this happen over and over again. The Fire-Aspect we're talking about here Exalted at 15-or-so less than a decade before he joins the circle.<br /> <br /> 4: He's really fucking bored and just joins them 'cause why the fuck not<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering why he would do this. What would drive a DB to join this Solar and Lunar? I don't want to use Solar brainwash bullshit or Lunar deception, I want this choice to be his own. Sorry if this has been discussed endlessly on the forum and I'm just wasting space.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe I am vastly overthinking a story where a major character is a Sidereal who owns a Starmetal kazoo</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Depends on how serious/dark you want this comedy to be. Assuming you want a relatively believable motive: While a Dynast gets everything they want from mortals, we cannot say the same for their friends (especially where other dynasts are involved). Maybe this DB had a close mortal friend who another DB decided needed to be dealt with in some manner? A family member who never Exalted? The Realm's got a lot of problems that a noble DB (going by the actual meaning of 'noble' here, not the bloodline version) could find abhorrent on a personal level.<br /> <br /> 2) I don't think he could learn the entire truth right off the bat, but he doesn't really have to. He could discover the Sidereals or something and learn from them if you really want to go that route, but if you don't want anyone else involved it could make sense for him to instead decide that the Realm's various platitudes (how the DBs aren't 100% noble and holy and the Anathema are not demons, for example, or how the war on the fringes is never meant to end) to be lies. (A Solar could offer himself for summary execution if you spare this village or whatever - there's a lot of ways to do this)<br /> <br /> 3) That goes both ways, though. Ten Winds had decades to overcome decades of immaculate philosophy, and as we saw with Karen in that same story, dogma is only so strong. If he's that young then his indoctrination probably isn't that strong as of yet. If he's confronted very quickly and often with how wrong he is about the Realm, then he could easily be shaken. Have a Lunar save his life or something, maybe?<br /> <br /> 4) ... Eh, sure, why not? You said this was a comedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:55:33-07:00","id":649342,"title":"","content":"We had a thread about this before. There's a bunch of reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. They could be a defector from decadence who decides that the Realm is simply unsalvageably corrupt and that they're better off siding with Anathema to purge the whole thing. An older DB might feel that this generation of Anathema, while dangerous, are still young and could be taught the right way to do things, whereas the Realm is too entrenched in its ways. (See eg. Barristan Selmy.)<br /> <br /> 2. A younger DB could feel the same way, and simply come to believe that these particular Anathema have the potential to make things better, or that they're simply better people than the families currently in control of the Realm. (eg. Zuko.)<br /> <br /> 3. They could be a total outcast in the Realm for any number of reasons -- or just have family issues or a personal grudge -- and side with Anathema for revenge. (eg. Tyrion Lannister, or Zuko again)<br /> <br /> 4. They could have been forced out of positions of power in the Realm somehow, and decided that siding with Anathema would be a way to get back into power while, probably, getting revenge on everyone. (eg. Tyrion Lannister again.)<br /> <br /> 5. They could side with the Anathema out of genuine bonds with them personally -- love, friendship, and so on. (See eg. Jorah Mormont.)<br /> <br /> (A lot of these depend on the DB having at least some inkling about Creation's true history, or at least having less-than-full confidence in the Immaculate dogma -- but I don't think that's uncommon. Few people know the FULL TRUTH, but I think just about any society has its skeptics, and any skeptic who thinks about it is eventually going to notice how self-serving Immaculate dogma on Anathema and the Dragon-Blooded is, which is at least a reason to approach it carefully. Even then, someone could side with Anathema for revenge, personal power, or even love while believing them to be soul-eating demons.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:05:50-07:00","id":649352,"title":"","content":"I point to Cynis Denovah Avaku's background; detailed in Scroll of Exalts. Not all Realm Dynasts have to come from the main dynastic households, but can come from a <i>comparatively</i> poor patrician cadet households and be <i>less </i>firmly indoctrinated in Dynast exceptionalism.<br /> <br /> Avaku <i>is </i>an young idealist who adheres to the morality of the Immaculate Philosophy; but Avaku once partook in a Wyld Hunt against an exalted child who was destroying Cynist drug shipments targeting that child's hometown. Avaku became all &quot;Is this how it should be?&quot; angsty over the matter (though quietly). [Re: the cartoon in the Second Edition handbook; pages 116-117.]<br /> <br /> His story is meant to demonstrate how even a Realm DB can have doubts and, if not be immediately sympathetic towards every Anathema they met, at least be <i>not fanatically </i>hostile, and so perhaps open to persuasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr </b>: There doesn't have to be a stark choice between fanatical Dynast DB and doubting Outcaste DB. There are middle grounds to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-02-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:33:53-07:00","id":649371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema#post649014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I love Exalted and read the books\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe me, I understand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema#post649014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm goes to <b>literally every length</b> possible to exult DB's as bodhisattvas who are <b>literally incapable of doing wrong</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, you're tossing around the L-bomb a little too freely. <br /> <br /> Second, this is untrue. DBs can absolutely fuck up. It's not that the DBs can do no wrong - it's that mortals cannot do wrong by obeying the orders of the Dragon-Blooded. If you're a mortal, and a DB tells you to do something, <i>that is the right thing to do</i>. <br /> <br /> It's pretty different from telling a DB they can do no wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-02-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:26:03-07:00","id":649511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649371#post649371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, you're tossing around the L-bomb a little too freely. </div> </div> </div> </div>Lesbians?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649371#post649371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believe me, I understand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second, this is untrue. DBs can absolutely fuck up. It's not that the DBs can do no wrong - it's that mortals cannot do wrong by obeying the orders of the Dragon-Blooded. If you're a mortal, and a DB tells you to do something, <i>that is the right thing to do</i>. <br /> <br /> It's pretty different from telling a DB they can do no wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really enforced much by the Order, though. At least not in any meaningful ways. Like if a dynast publicly flays a peasant alive the Order's gonna cluck it's tongue and shake it's head and condemn it, but they're probably not going to send a bunch of monks to go Kung-fu fight the guy for his excesses. If they were killing whole towns then yeah they totally would, but that's more in the interest of keeping the empire sound. It's like the Templar you always see in stories about the crusades who get that pre-forgiveness crap that absolves the, from present and future sins during the battle and subsequent sacking of the city. <br /> <br /> In fact that kind of behaviour might be the thing to drive a lone DB over the edge and out of the Realm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:38:08-07:00","id":649523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649511#post649511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesbians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who'd make a bomb out of lesbians?<br /> <br /> ... Or are the bombs lesbians? Who gives a bomb a gender, let alone a libido?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:40:31-07:00","id":649525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649511#post649511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesbians?</div> </div> </div> </div>See the parts of the quote I bolded. The <i>only</i> word starting with an &quot;L&quot; that's in both bolded parts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">The relatively recent use of the word &quot;literally&quot; to mean precisely the opposite of its understood meaning vexes me so much that I've resolved to drastically cut down on my own use of the word.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-02-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:45:00-07:00","id":649528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649523#post649523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who gives a bomb a gender, let alone a libido?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who gives <i>you</i> a gender and libido? Jeez, HT, let the bomb decide what she identifies as! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:48:36-07:00","id":649531,"title":"","content":"<i>Everyone</i> knows what you meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"than