let alone a libido?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something the Twilight Sorceress I mentioned earlier would make.<br /> <br /> I've been wracking my mind to come up with some absurd/funny artifacts, incidentally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:01:17-07:00","id":649544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649531#post649531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Everyone</i> knows what you meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to be sure, man. Poe's Law and all. Next time include a smiley. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T20:34:46-07:00","id":649712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649523#post649523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who'd make a bomb out of lesbians?<br /> <br /> ... Or are the bombs lesbians? Who gives a bomb a gender, let alone a libido?</div> </div> </div> </div>Smart Bombs need lovin' too...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I'll show myself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T20:45:32-07:00","id":649721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649511#post649511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really enforced much by the Order, though. At least not in any meaningful ways. Like if a dynast publicly flays a peasant alive the Order's gonna cluck it's tongue and shake it's head and condemn it, but they're probably not going to send a bunch of monks to go Kung-fu fight the guy for his excesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. Page 89 of Compass: Blessed Isle talks about how the Immaculates have led resistance, both passive and active, against tyrants.<br /> <br /> I definitely remember reading a specific story about a particular uprising against injustice fronted by the Order, but cannot find the citation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T03:46:54-07:00","id":649907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649523#post649523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who'd make a bomb out of lesbians?<br /> <br /> ... Or are the bombs lesbians? Who gives a bomb a gender, let alone a libido?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... this could work in Autochthonia... with a truly demented Apostate. Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:55:28-07:00","id":649991,"title":"","content":"Something I'm using myself, but as it might give some ideas... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In a story I poke around with from time to time, I have a Dynast DB that will join up with a circle of Solars. During an ad-hoc Wyld Hunt (she and the hunt commander being the only DBs, and a bunch of mortal troops), her Patrician lover, whom she had personally recommended as part of the mortal force, exalted as a Solar while saving the life of the Wyld Hunt commander. The Wyld Hunt commander missed that part, and as the two Solars took off, he thought his troops had ran them off and it all was an attempt on his life. So she had to flee for her life, and her only chance of clearing her name is to find those Solars and prove she isn't a traitor and an Anathema collaborator. So the progression will be &quot;enemies&quot; -&gt; &quot;uneasy alliance as she is as hunted as them&quot; -&gt; &quot;friends and allies&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:56:24-07:00","id":650309,"title":"","content":"Okay, here are some other options for ya.<br /> <br /> 1: Rebellious Phase: Dynast kids don't have a lot of freedom. Their lives are very strictly managed from the time they are tiny...and it isn't until after they finish all of their schooling that they get a modicum of freedom. Take a look at some examples of where stuff like this has happened in the real world...specifically 'Disney Kids.' Child actors for Disney have a very tightly controlled life. They aren't allowed to be crazy, they aren't allowed to get into trouble...they are watched too closely for that. So, very often, when they get too old for Disney and the restraints go away.....you get Miley Cyrus randomly licking things and rubbing her butt on Mexican flags. So, it could be that your 20-something Dragonblooded has been controlled and regulated their entire life, and now that they FINALLY have some freedom, they went: F*#k it, I'm going to go have an Adventure! With people that my family would disapprove of! Because I F%#king Can!<br /> <br /> 2: The Skeptic: There are a good number of people who have been raised to a particular belief system and have come to a point in their life where they re-examine what they believe. They ask the question: &quot;Do I actually believe this, or am I just going with what I was taught?&quot; This often happens late teens to twenties (not to be confused with rebelling because you are a teenager...this is a thoughtful examination of your worldview). This is when they take a step back and try to figure out if they actually agree with what they have been taught their entire life, and decide if they are going to stick with it or not. The impetus for this is usually when something happens that challenges their view of the world; for a silly example, suppose you were taught your entire life that the Earth was flat, and today you got on a plane and could see the curvature of the planet. So, your character could be a DB who is either actively re-examining the Immaculate Philosophy, or has gone over it and found it wanting. You don't have to be hundreds of years old to run into something that upsets your view of how the world should work, after all. And there are plenty of people out there who would prefer to think about it for themselves rather than just running to whoever taught them to plead for explanations. Or, this could be someone who is simply extremely logical and wants to see both sides of the story.<br /> <br /> 3: The Plant: The Dragonblood may not even know it...but he's a plant. Either through high-powered brainwashing charms (the Dynasty tree has some nasty ones, IIRC), or indoctrination, or some other method...this character believes that they want to join the Anathema for whatever reason. The real reason is because they are a spy and/or a betrayal bomb. At a given command or signal, their 'programming' kicks in and they betray the party....or maybe they have 'strange dreams' where they are actually reporting their actions to a Sidereal observer (Quicksilver Hand of Dreams Style would be good at this). In short...they are with the party because someone more powerful than them manipulated them into it. Of course, because Solar...it's very possible that the brainwashing may be discovered and undone before it is triggered....causing the DB to be outraged at how their own family manipulated them...turning them into an example of Idea 2.<br /> <br /> 4: Solar Cheese: Solars can brainwash you. By accident, sometimes. They are just that charismatic. You could have a devout Dragonblooded who is an ardent follower of the Immaculate Philosophy...and then a Solar Social Monster wanders by and blows that intimacy into itty bitty pieces as collateral damage to a speech they are giving about revising tax law or something.<br /> <br /> 5: Lunar Cheese: Lunars can brainwash you and make you think it was your idea in the first place. See above.<br /> <br /> And, of course, all of the other things people have said before me.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T19:44:42-07:00","id":650861,"title":"","content":"The most obvious option is &quot;There is something threatening that I can't take care of myself but may be able to take care of with these Anathema that I distrust more then I distrust them&quot;- be that stupid Scarlet Empress + Ebon Dragon insanity or generic army who is against me. Most Dragon-Blooded are loyal to the Realm/Immaculate Philosophy, but save for the dedicated few, they're loyal to simply living more. &quot;I'll work with (that evil) now, and then kill them later&quot; has probably indeed been a philosophy used many a time. Probably, it's even succeeded.<br /> <br /> There's also the &quot;I see a Solar Anathema, I report back to the Wyld Hunt, then I smile and play nice until the Wyld Hunt arrives to kill them as I can't do it alone but want them tracked&quot;- probably not the best option for a game that's not intended on breaking out in to player-versus-player conflict, but works for a story. Also works for any member of the All Seeing Eye (we need to know what the Anathema and their friends are up to before we kill it!).<br /> <br /> Jadedness is also a reason: a Heptagram graduate or a member of House Leedal may be a bit more aware of Sidereals then they might 'supposed' to be, and their reaction may be more &quot;Eh, let's see what this one does and if I can use it&quot; then &quot;ZOMG KILL ON SIGHT&quot;. Actually, that works for really any jaded person, ever. Many Dragon-Blooded believe in the Immaculate Philosophy, but in terms of 3E, wouldn't have an intimacy towards it: a detached sort of &quot;Let's see if I can turn the Anathema to my own uses and win power/love/fame in the Realm later&quot; works.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, social-fu. Any Celestial Exalt has their own ways of making one loyal through charms. Some won't even need charms, just some contested rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1374-mikka","name":"Mikka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:00:01-07:00","id":650908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649528#post649528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who gives <i>you</i> a gender and libido? Jeez, HT, let the bomb decide what she identifies as! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) You didn't either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) We already established the bomb was a lesbian, so by definition, it's a she<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=649907#post649907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually... this could work in Autochthonia... with a truly demented Apostate. Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well... here's the thing.<br /> <br /> If you make a bomb out of lesbians, you're not gonna get much yield. The human body isn't know for being filled with TNT.<br /> <br /> If you give a bomb a gender, that means it could potentially reproduce. Even if you make them lesbians as often as possible, sooner or later there's gonna be a mutation that makes it straight, or essence will clump together in a way that makes it reproduce asexually. And that means more bombs that are more likely to reproduce than the last batch, etc etc. (Sure, there might not be any male bombs, but find a particularly clever demon and suddenly you do)<br /> <br /> And presumably you made this bomb in a way that means it WANTS to blow things up. Which means you now have an entire race of bombs that are just LOOKING for things to blow up while also reproducing. Even if the entire world isn't destroyed, you're gonna see some serious damage. That's part of the trouble with bioweapons, after all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:33:08-07:00","id":650923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=650908#post650908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, well... here's the thing.<br /> <br /> If you make a bomb out of lesbians, you're not gonna get much yield. The human body isn't know for being filled with TNT.<br /> <br /> If you give a bomb a gender, that means it could potentially reproduce. Even if you make them lesbians as often as possible, sooner or later there's gonna be a mutation that makes it straight, or essence will clump together in a way that makes it reproduce asexually. And that means more bombs that are more likely to reproduce than the last batch, etc etc. (Sure, there might not be any male bombs, but find a particularly clever demon and suddenly you do)<br /> <br /> And presumably you made this bomb in a way that means it WANTS to blow things up. Which means you now have an entire race of bombs that are just LOOKING for things to blow up while also reproducing. Even if the entire world isn't destroyed, you're gonna see some serious damage. That's part of the trouble with bioweapons, after all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see this conversation and can only think of Bombette and the Bomb-ombs from Paper Mario walking around Creation causing trouble...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T23:38:43-07:00","id":650951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=650908#post650908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human body isn't know for being filled with TNT.</div> </div> </div> </div>If even bombs can be lesbians, why are you assuming that a given group of lesbians must be human?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=650908#post650908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you give a bomb a gender, that means it could potentially reproduce.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gender&quot; refers more to the social and cultural expectations of male and female than the physical appearance (or even existence) of one's wobbly bits; as such, no, a gendered bomb is not magically able to sexually reproduce (or at least, no more so than a non-gendered bomb).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:22:42-07:00","id":651150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=650923#post650923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this conversation and can only think of Bombette and the Bomb-ombs from Paper Mario walking around Creation causing trouble...</div> </div> </div> </div>yyyup...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=650951#post650951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If even bombs can be lesbians, why are you assuming that a given group of lesbians must be human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Gender&quot; refers more to the social and cultural expectations of male and female than the physical appearance (or even existence) of one's wobbly bits; as such, no, a gendered bomb is not magically able to sexually reproduce (or at least, no more so than a non-gendered bomb). </div> </div> </div>No, gender is a synonym for sex (mostly, anyway - it can't be used as a verb). Masculine/feminine refers to social/cultural expectations of a given gender.<br /> <br /> Also, you knew exactly what I meant &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:33:57-07:00","id":651160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=651150#post651150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, gender is a synonym for sex</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite incorrect.<br /> <br /> Sex, gender, and orientation are all totally different concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:05:07-07:00","id":651201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=651160#post651160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is quite incorrect.<br /> <br /> Sex, gender, and orientation are all totally different concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>gender </b>gen\u00b7der (j\u011bn'd\u0259r) <br /> <i>n. </i><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The sex of an individual, male or female, based on reproductive anatomy.</li> <li>Sexual identity, especially in relation to society or culture.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> So... yes, it can be used in this context.<br /> <br /> And you knew what context I was using it in.<br /> <br /> Think I'm done with this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:14:12-07:00","id":651211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https: