iv class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652643#post652643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had my dynast stumble into heaven itself during the Carnival of Meeting and get stranded there for a few months.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did all the gods sneer at and shun your dynast because he could never Exalt as a Celestial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:27:46-07:00","id":652698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652688#post652688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I bet the Sidereals were <b><i>thrilled</i></b> about that.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't at all put it past the Bronze Faction to just assassinate any DB who did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's notions like this in the books that needs to be shot behind the chemical shed and dumped in a lime pit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:36:19-07:00","id":652699,"title":"","content":"Why?<br /> <br /> A DB in Heaven can easily find out the Immaculate faith is a bunch of lies. And find out about the Sidereals. That is a serious problem, because not all of them will be OK with living out lies and being used by the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem is finding out where all the Sidereals live and work. What if the the Dragon-Blooded host one day decide they're sick of being manipulated and it's time for another Usurpation? Perhaps they can't take down the whole Bureau of Destiny because of all the godly allies Sidereals have, but they could surely do some terrible damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652693#post652693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did all the gods sneer at and shun your dynast because he could never Exalt as a Celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>This, on the other hand, was a dumb thing to put in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:41:13-07:00","id":652706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652699#post652699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, on the other hand, was a dumb thing to put in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is I was joking. I agree with Zelbinnean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:44:32-07:00","id":652712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652688#post652688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I bet the Sidereals were <b><i>thrilled</i></b> about that.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't at all put it past the Bronze Faction to just assassinate any DB who did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was chasing a Solar Pirate. The entire affair looked like a Scooby-Doo cartoon chase.<br /> <br /> I think they mostly left her well enough alone because finding out the truth drove her mad, and she kept on beating up people who interfered with her insane giggling time.<br /> Then she was a pupil of Five Days Darkness, rendered untouchable. The fact she is a Ledaal probably helped matters when she came back to the Realm, though she's still basically a Persona Non Grata sent out to live out the rest of her days off in the ass end of the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:49:01-07:00","id":652714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652693#post652693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did all the gods sneer at and shun your dynast because he could never Exalt as a Celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they sneered at her because she was a haughty Immaculate and then they shunned her because she'd occasionally break their digits. Either for sneering at her or trying to arrest her.<br /> <br /> Trying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:49:24-07:00","id":652715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Mnemon absolutely knows about Sidereals, which is why Kejak doesn't want her on the throne.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I recall, the issue is that Mnemon doesn't know the whole story, and Chejop and other Sidereals are reluctant to fill her in on any more of it. I think this is supposed to be an issue they have with <i>any</i> Dynasts who know about Sidereals; nobody is supposed to have ever known as much about it as the Empress (for instance, Mnemon knows that there are Sidereals and knows that the other Exalted aren't genuinely soul-eating demon sorcerer things, but I don't think she's supposed to be aware that the entire Immaculate Philosophy is a fabrication of the Sidereals, which could be a problem), and there are a few problems with having somebody else know as much (which range from the possibility that it will undermine their ability to work in the system, since people who have grown up in the Realm probably can't appreciate the context before it that made the system seem necessary, to the idea that the Sidereals would prefer somebody who could be more easily directed than the Empress was). I It's a complex issue. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are heavily censored - for patricians.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I recall for <i>that</i>, it's more that they're abridged than they are censored. For example, patricians get told a story about Eyem that heavily abstract a lot of the details of how it actually manipulated House Jerah, and leave out describing it as a thinking automaton. They get told a polemic, while the Exalted get something like a technical description. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think most accessible ancient sorcerous times would have been heavily censored millennia ago.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well sure. It's just that it's sometimes necessary or unavoidable that somebody reads something that isn't. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">whenever the books have explained about how the mysterious and secretive master trainers at the Heptagram and Cloister use powers DBs can't... it's also kind of stupid. Surely the DBs would be suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't know what sources you're thinking of here, but I'm willing to chalk that up mostly to some freelancers running with something a bit past consistency with the rest of the setting. The idea of Sidereals as secret tutors is fine when it runs with the idea that most of their powers for such will not be giving themselves away and that the Dynasty regularly employs mortal tutors. Maybe also the idea that members of the Dynasty are aware that weird, inexplicable things and people exist in the world, and that they will encounter them sometimes. The key is to keep in mind that Ledaal Kes using the term &quot;Five-Score Fellowship&quot; does not mean that he has access to a copy of Exalted: the Sidereals; indeed, thinking of them as Realm patriots alone strongly implies that there are serious gaps in his understanding of them. Other than that, I think a lot of people interact with Sidereals the way that characters in The Lord of the Rings interact with Gandalf; they're not generally very curious about where he came from as opposed to what he's doing at the moment, and they're typically all right (if a bit cordially frustrated) with the idea that any questions about such will be met with cryptic or obstinate responses. (I think a lot of audience members are like this as well; as far as I know, the general moviegoing public took the idea of Gandalf as a largely uncategorized thing and that whole matter of <i>returning from the dead</i> at face value)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:52:25-07:00","id":652719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652706#post652706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is I was joking. I agree with Zelbinnean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean who ever heard of a Sidereals killing people to protect their secrets? It's not like we're describing a group of people who's committed far worse in the name of a purported greater good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T10:39:37-07:00","id":652763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652699#post652699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?<br /> <br /> A DB in Heaven can easily find out the Immaculate faith is a bunch of lies. And find out about the Sidereals. That is a serious problem, because not all of them will be OK with living out lies and being used by the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's terribly boring as a blanket policy statement, for one thing. And it's a pretty lazy policy, for another. It's an example of something that is really heavy-handed and shuts down stories.<br /> <br /> I think it's more interesting to want to manipulate, explain away, rationalize, and justify it to any DB you see. Present them with the factual choice that if they go home and tell everyone, who will actually believe them? They'll be called a heretic and killed. And if they are believed by some few, what will it accomplish rather than push the Sick Man that is the Realm right over the precipice due to anarchy in its top rank? Or get you labeled &quot;dangerous to the ongoing order of the Realm&quot; and either exiled or given a truly shit position as far away from anything important as possible to keep you quiet? Or say you actually agree with that, then go home and double cross the agreement - that kicks off additional plots.<br /> <br /> That is a choice and the seed of a story. &quot;lol teacup ninja leaps forth from your bowl of pho at a canal-side noodle shop and kills u with ur own chopstix bc your punk ass shouldn't be here, gg, reroll a new char&quot; is not.<br /> <br /> Of course Sids can kill DBs - and probably without too much difficulty, given the right agent or just the right martial arts. How exactly is that interesting? What value does that add to the setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652699#post652699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger problem is finding out where all the Sidereals live and work. What if the the Dragon-Blooded host one day decide they're sick of being manipulated and it's time for another Usurpation? Perhaps they can't take down the whole Bureau of Destiny because of all the godly allies Sidereals have, but they could surely do some terrible damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how DBs can't open gates to Yu-Shan on their own, let alone know where they are, lol good luck with that, and I am sure Heaven is just going to sit idly by while the Realm invades it, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T11:08:39-07:00","id":652805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I bet the Sidereals were thrilled about that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would not find it the least bit implausible for an event like that to happen and no Sidereals even knew about it. Heaven is enormous. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A DB in Heaven can easily find out the Immaculate faith is a bunch of lies.</div> </div> </div> </div> <u>Can</u> find out? Sure. Can <i>easily</i> find out? Are they having casual conversations with Celestial gods in which they ask what it's like for the Dragon Blooded to be the pinnacle of enlightenment? And then belieiving those gods if they should decide to say &quot;actually, your religion is made up&quot;. And then what, is that Dynast going to head back and tell others about it in a way that's believed? Carnival of Meeting or no, I imagine that for the vast majority of people, even a lot of the Exalted, stories of visiting Yu-Shan are the local equivalent to alien abduction tales. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the the Dragon-Blooded host one day decide they're sick of being manipulated and it's time for another Usurpation?</div> </div> </div> </div> They're going to be pretty embarressed when they all pack themselves into a tight corridor and find that they can't even get past the doors. Yu-Shan is not easily invaded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:36:10-07:00","id":652969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652805#post652805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would not find it the least bit implausible for an event like that to happen and no Sidereals even knew about it. Heaven is enormous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, this is one reason why it doesn't shut down stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652763#post652763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how DBs can't open gates to Yu-Shan on their own, let alone know where they are, lol good luck with that, and I am sure Heaven is just going to sit idly by while the Realm invades it, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is new information to me and makes your position more plausible.<br /> <br /> I still think that the Bronze Faction would be <i><b>very concerned</b></i> by Dragon-Blooded (or Lunars) getting into Yu-Shan and would definitely assassinate someone if they learned something they shouldn't, unless they can be manipulated into not stirring the pot, and/or are too important to the Realm to just eliminate.<br /> <br /> It's not like the Bronze are shy about murdering people who merely might be a threat to their agenda. It's implausible to me that ethical considerations, for example, would matter at all in the consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:44:05-07:00","id":652977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652969#post652969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think that the Bronze Faction would be <i><b>very concerned</b></i> by Dragon-Blooded (or Lunars) getting into Yu-Shan and would definitely assassinate someone if they learned something they shouldn't, unless they can be manipulated into not stirring the pot, and/or are too important to the Realm to just eliminate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are hugely overestimating how dangerous information from heaven might be to the institutions of the Realm. Of course a wayward god might tell a visiting Dynast that the Immaculate Philosophy is a tissue of lies and reveal the secret history of Creation, but so might many demons conjured by Heptagram sorcerers. Even if the claims are given credence, a single disillusioned Dynast would be hard pressed to erode centuries of tradition by spreading such obvious heresy.<br /> <br /> More to the point, the Realm is not a theocratic state and there are already many secular Dynasts who doubt the truth of the Philosophy. They have no particular reason to challenge its claims or to refrain from cynically exploiting the worldly benefits of a religion which idealizes them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:47:40-07:00","id":653003,"title":"","content":"I think most would continue taking advantage of their worldly power. I don't think most would appreciate being manipulated by Sidereals, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:12:23-07:00","id":653023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652969#post652969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like the Bronze are shy about murdering people who merely might be a threat to their agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that should also be less of a thing, for the reason that it's pretty boring if half of a playable splat are pretty much exclusively portrayed as one-note hardline assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:14:36-07:00","id":653025,"title":"","content":"Conveniently, the magic that made the world forget the existence of the Sidereal Exalted is still in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:21:58-07:00","id":653028,"title":"","content":"That only protects individuals from being remembered. It doesn't stop Dragon-Blooded (who have the capacity to pierce Arcane Fate anyway) from remembering that Sidereals in general exist and are dicking around the Realm for unclear motives. It does make it hard to find and identify and target a particular Sidereal, but the problem isn't solely &quot;DBs are gonna kill Sidereals if they find out!&quot; It's also the potential for them to get more deliberately resistant to manipulation,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653023#post653023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that should also be less of a thing, for the reason that it's pretty boring if half of a playable splat are pretty much exclusively portrayed as one-note hardline assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be good, yes! Although several things that have resulted from their actions would have to change as well. &quot;The ends justify the means.&quot; has shaped all they've done in a big enough way that some of the setting's history would have to be rewritten.<br /> <br /> However if all it takes is one Sidereal to assassinate someone, then it only takes one who decides that someone is worth assassinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:34:52-07:00","id":653035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652715#post652715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that, I think a lot of people interact with Sidereals the way that characters in The Lord of the Rings interact with Gandalf; they're not generally very curious about where he came from as opposed to what he's doing at the moment, and they're typically all right (if a bit cordially frustrated) with the idea that any questions about such will be met with cryptic or obstinate responses. (I think a lot of audience members are like this as well; as far as I know, the general moviegoing public took the idea of Gandalf as a largely uncategorized thing and that whole matter of <i>returning from the dead</i> at face value)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. In LotR, wizards were an established thing -- people had sayings and stories about them. They might not know everything about the technical details, but when Gandalf appeared and started throwing around magic, they'd say &quot;oh, it's a <i>wizard</i>, everyone knows what a wizard is.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the audience it's much the same. Gandalf has a long white beard, a pointy hat, a robe, and a staff. Of course he can use magic. Why wouldn't he be able to? What else is there to explain? <i>Pointy hat. Beard.</i> QED.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are in a more awkward position because there's no easy explanation for the powers they wield, no easy cultural narrative they can slip into to make people accept them without question. They can pass themselves off as mortal sorcerers, perhaps, or (in 3e) as Exigents, but these wouldn't have worked as well in 2e, and anyone who witnesses Sidereal powers too frequently or used by multiple different Sidereals is going to start to get suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:01:28-07:00","id":653119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653028#post653028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That only protects individuals from being remembered. It doesn't stop Dragon-Blooded (who have the capacity to pierce Arcane Fate anyway) from remembering that Sidereals in general exist and are dicking around the Realm for unclear motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain this is wrong. If it isn't then the Lunars really are fucking morons because they've had hundreds of years where they could've exploited this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-05-2015, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:18:25-07:00","id":653127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653119#post653119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain this is wrong. If it isn't then the Lunars really are fucking morons because they've had hundreds of years where they could've exploited this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the lack of this one missed opportunity can save 2E Lunars from being do-nothing morons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think the Arcane Fate destroys <i><b>written</b></i> records about Sidereals in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653023#post653023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that should also be less of a thing, for the reason that it's pretty boring if half of a playable splat are pretty much exclusively portrayed as one-note hardline assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it more, this isn't really any different from Realm Dynasts... and the loyalist Infernals and Abyssals are significantly worse.<br /> <br /> One-note is boring. I don't think there's a total lack of individual variation in any of those splats in terms of what they're willing to do, or even what their motivations are. But as Exalted hosts, the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded play the role in the setting of defending and benefitting from the status quo, which means that as groups they include lots of people, and policies, that condone and/or encourage what the status quo is and does -- much of which is quite awful. Maintaining an empire and slave trade requires routine acts of extreme brutality and cruelty. Maintaining the Wyld Hunt requires being willing to murder people who haven't done anything to earn death. Getting things done in Heaven and the Realm often involves graft and dirty dealing.<br /> <br /> Individual characters can act against the grain, but part of being a member of groups that have this narrative role is that they will be connected with, involved in, complicit with, or asked to participate in &quot;asshole&quot; activities. Whether they believe it's justified or not, how they go about their business in that context, and what goals they have, that looks to me like part of roleplaying in the context of that narrative role in the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-05-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:28:57-07:00","id":653137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In LotR, wizards were an established thing -- people had sayings and stories about them. They might not know everything about the technical details, but when Gandalf appeared and started throwing around magic, they'd say &quot;oh, it's a wizard, everyone knows what a wizard is.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> People have sayings about wizards because the five wizards in the world have been around for two thousand years. I doubt anybody had any homiles about Gandalf being subtle and quick to anger when he was fresh off the boat. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are in a more awkward position because there's no easy explanation for the powers they wield, no easy cultural narrative they can slip into to make people accept them without question.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's basically what Arcane Fate does, doesn't it? People just kind of ascribe the Sidereal whatever narrative seems most intuitive (often guided if they're wearing a resplendent destiny), only for it to be quickly forgotten and break down entirely if it's thought about for five minutes. Much like Gandalf; dress him up properly, and most people's first impression will be &quot;wizard&quot;, never stopping to question how that actually works in the greater established context. Look at Avoidance Kata; the whole thing of &quot;just disappear; they'll come up with their own explanation&quot;. Again, all keeping in mind that most Sidereal powers will not be apparent to anybody; what exactly is the Sidereal tutor doing that the Dynast questions in the first place? Mnemon only suspected there was something up with her martial arts instructor when he vanished in front of her under exceptional circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:33:10-07:00","id":653140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653137#post653137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon only suspected there was something up with her martial arts instructor when he vanished in front of her under exceptional circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought she eventually saw a caste mark -- was that later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:49:32-07:00","id":653492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653137#post653137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> basically what Arcane Fate does, doesn't it? People just kind of ascribe the Sidereal whatever narrative seems most intuitive (often guided if they're wearing a resplendent destiny), only for it to be quickly forgotten and break down entirely if it's thought about for five minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make people ascribe them a narrative (that's only with the destiny... although the fluff sometimes seems to think it does), it just makes people forget about them.<br /> Of course, that would work fine, if a DB pupil wonders why his sifu never flares or uses common DB charms, but then forgets about it. He's unlikely to just punch him in the face without thinking things through just because something's odd, as long as the Sidereal doesn't actually flare his castemark (I'm sure I recall one book where the Sidereals at the Heptagram all wore masks to avoid showing their mark).<br /> Essentially, I think the Sidereals could stay completely hidden, if the writing was changed a bit (which 3rd ed should give the opportunity for).<br /> Honestly, it's not like it's really that necessary for Sidereals to be teaching at the Heptagram or Cloister.<br /> <br /> Although, on the other hand, I kind of like the idea that some of the top DBs just know that Sidereals exist and work with them, because why not use every tool you can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-06-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:01:26-07:00","id":653503,"title":"","content":"A few pages ago, people were talking about dynasts in Yu-Shan.<br /> I played a game \u200bonce where our Dynastic PCs accidentally ended up in Yu-Shan. Sidereals didn't try and murder us, I guess why bother? Actually, we didn't see or learn anything about Sidereals (we learnt about them later when we were in a Sidereal prison, that's when we decided we needed to murder them all because we learnt they'd even infiltrated the most holy Immaculate Order!).<br /> <br /> We did learn that DBs weren't really reincarnations of very righteous people, but just some random person. This was a horrifying sign of how incompetent and corrupt the Gods were, not doing the job the Dragons had commanded them to do (they also wouldn't admit that the Dragons were in charge, or indeed we were the Princes of the Earth - the disrespectful curs).<br /> <br /> Of course, some of the PCs were already cynical and jaded, and weren't that bothered to find out part of their religion was wrong. They just tried to see if they could use Parad's department to make sure their own kids exalted.<br /> Some, as I said, put this down to corrupt Gods.<br /> And one decided to start a conspiracy to invade Yu-Shan, tear down the sun itself, and build a new Heaven upon the ruins of the old, breaking Fate and allowing men to write their own destiny (he, as an officer, was extremely upset by the War Fate-planning committee, probably more than by the reincarnation issue).<br /> <br /> The first time I read about Getimians, I just thought, &quot;Hey, they're stealing Tepet Nether's schtick!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-06-2015, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:03:49-07:00","id":653651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't make people ascribe them a narrative (that's only with the destiny... although the fluff sometimes seems to think it does), it just makes people forget about them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was thinking about the part where it makes it really easy for a Sidereal to disguise themselves. Arcane Fate isn't just about people forgetting you when you're gone, it's about them getting virtually no impression of you as a person when you're right in front of them; you're there, but they don't really get a read on you or sense of something distinct, so they just take you at face value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:10:38-07:00","id":653658,"title":"","content":"Maybe? Maybe not. I mean, yeah, it gives you a bonus to disguise and stealth because of that, but it's not really explained in great detail how it works in a social sense. Do they take you at face value? Do they just ignore you? I don't feel it's well-explained.<br /> Honestly, I'm looking forward to a better-explained Arcane Fate in this edition.<br /> <br /> In terms of them teaching at the Heptagram/Cloister, however, I assume they have to use a Resplendent Destiny, since otherwise their students would constantly forget to come and be taught by them. As a teacher, I can tell you it's hard enough to get students to remember the homework you gave them at the best of times! It would be incredibly awkward if every time my students turned up, they only vaguely remembered me. And when you have less students, and a more individual-tutor style, them remembering you is even more important, because it's helpful that they understand you and know you well, so they can get the most use out of your teaching. They need to know and trust that they can ask you questions, they need to know what things you're an expert on and what you're not, and so forth.\u200b<br /> <br /> For an inspector or auditor who turns up, sits at the back and watches, it would be fine however. This is why I think Sidereals running the Heptagram/Cloister from behind the scenes, rather than as tutors, works better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-06-2015, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:40:19-07:00","id":653679,"title":"","content":"IRC, in 1e, the effect of people looking at a Sidereal and thinking &quot;wizard&quot;, without thinking too much about the details of what exact kind of Exalt they were, was achieved in theory by them donning the resplendent destiny of the Sorcerer. However much in the way of teeth this actually had as mechanics.<br /> <br /> In context of this, I sort of wonder whether the 3e Heptagram will recruit &quot;mortal&quot; sorcerors to act as advisors and teachers, or whether Immaculate and Dynastic ideology would still prevent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:57:27-07:00","id":653693,"title":"","content":"Officially, they're not allowed to.<br /> Though theologically, monks could in theory do it (they're allowed to deal with magic, spirits, etc), they just don't. I guess the Heptagram could have special Monk-sorcerers (that are really Sidereals).<br /> <br /> As I said though, I feel Sidereals teaching Dragonblood terrestrial spells is a bit of a waste. So they might as well stick to running things behind the scenes as servants, assistants, teachers of theology and history, etc, which doesn't require them to use sorcery in front of Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-06-2015, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T04:05:42-07:00","id":653697,"title":"","content":"Hah, sorry, by &quot;mortal&quot; (in quotes) I didn't mean Sidereals but literally what we could call mortal sorcerers, with added quotes due to &quot;Are sorcerers even mortal any more?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T04:14:11-07:00","id":653699,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. Yeah, I think unless there's a really pressing reason, it's too much against Immaculate theology (except, as I said, for Monks, but they don't generally learn sorcery).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T05:00:01-07:00","id":653747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema#post649014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a DB of the Realm join a group of Anathema?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're a-holes, but they're not 100% dicks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T05:54:36-07:00","id":653775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652763#post652763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how DBs can't open gates to Yu-Shan on their own, let alone know where they are, lol good luck with that, and I am sure Heaven is just going to sit idly by while the Realm invades it, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=652969#post652969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now this is new information to me and makes your position more plausible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely, but pretty close. <br /> <br /> It only takes <i>Open the Spirit Door,</i> a spell of the Emerald Circle, to enter the corridor from Creation (and there is one gate on the Isle where this is not even needed), then 60+ levels of post soak damage to breach the gates at the other end, or twice that to break them open, all the while holding off Celestial Lion guards. But they do have a rather lot of soak.<br /> <br /> Thus, although it is obviously in no way easy, it is not totally <i>impossible</i> for dragon-blooded to force their way through. <br /> <br /> Of course, this all requires an element of complete surprise. Otherwise, if the gates are sealed, as they were during the Balorian Invasion, then <i>nobody</i> can enter. Not merely not the Dragon-blooded; <i>nobody</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T07:43:18-07:00","id":653909,"title":"","content":"Ah I was thinking the CCS gate-summoning spell. My mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:07:00-07:00","id":654050,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine the DBs ever wanting to risk going to heaven. They're considered property there aren't they? Like if a god scoops them up off the street they're subject to finders laws and now belong to said God. That's one hell of a bad end, depending on the god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:14:54-07:00","id":654058,"title":"","content":"Property? What?<br /> That can't be true. Even Dragon Kings have more rights in Heaven than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:26:58-07:00","id":654066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=653775#post653775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only takes <i>Open the Spirit Door,</i> a spell of the Emerald Circle, to enter the corridor from Creation (and there is one gate on the Isle where this is not even needed), then 60+ levels of post soak damage to breach the gates at the other end, or twice that to break them open, all the while holding off Celestial Lion guards. But they do have a rather lot of soak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read the section on Spirit Doors in the White Treatise and it DOES include Yu-Shan. That's kind of crazy.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Eclipse: &quot;Hey! There's another one of those weird gates! I wonder if I can open it.&quot; *opens Yu-Shan Gate*<br /> Sorcerous Eclipse: &quot;Wow... This is a long scary tunnel. I wonder what I will find at the other end!&quot; *met Celestial Lion*<br /> Celestial Lion: &quot;Hello, Nosy Naru. Welcome to Yu-Shan. It has been quite a while since we have hosted one of the Quills of Heaven.&quot;<br /> Sorcerous Eclipse: *enters the glorious City of Gods* &quot;Sweet!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-06-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:35:25-07:00","id":654076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654058#post654058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Property? What?<br /> That can't be true. Even Dragon Kings have more rights in Heaven than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being UCS worshipers, there's a reason for that.<br /> <br /> Bad fluff is also bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:01:11-07:00","id":654372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654058#post654058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Property? What?<br /> That can't be true. Even Dragon Kings have more rights in Heaven than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, but as Zel pointed out they worship the UCS above all else. Sadly mortal humans and terrestrial exalted are not extended the same courtesy. its mega dangerous for even a high ranking DB to go there, I'm not even sure that the Empress would be given and kind of exception. You might think that it's not too bad because they're still exalted and after all it'd take a badass God to mess with the Empress. The thing is the law is not on their side, so if some God grabs them and says &quot;gotcha, mine now, finders keepers.&quot; The celestial lions will enforce that ownership.<br /> <br /> Probably changing next edition though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:10:25-07:00","id":654418,"title":"","content":"The way the game all but says at numerous points, &quot;Dragon Blooded aren't <i>real</i> Exalted,&quot; is probably the single biggest bit of bullshit in the Exalted gameline and the thing I dislike above anything else. It will <i>definitely</i> be getting changed in 3rd edition because Holden and Morke have both noted how cancerous that idea was to the gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:27:27-07:00","id":654429,"title":"","content":"The idea was more complicated than &quot;Dragon Blooded belong to the first god who claims them&quot;. It was a bit crudely stated, but the idea was that if a Terrestrial was in Heaven then they had to have the accompaniment of somebody else who had responsibility for what they do. In some ways, that could be advantageous; an offence below what you could be summarily executed for is one that your companion will have to answer for, and a lot of non-judicial harm inflicted on you can be construed as an offence against them. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the game all but says at numerous points, &quot;Dragon Blooded aren't real Exalted,&quot; is probably the single biggest bit of bullshit in the Exalted gameline and the thing I dislike above anything else</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on whether or not one considers the category of Exalted to exclude something like real life caste sensibilities. I actually like the image of the First Age applying a sense of the Terrestrial Exalted as the Kshatriyas to the Celestial Brahmins, with the idea that no matter how acclaimed and respected a soldier you are there are just some things and places where it is sacrilige for you to do or go. Characters and societies having attitudes within the setting does not equate to an endorsement by the game. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will definitely be getting changed in 3rd edition because Holden and Morke have both noted how cancerous that idea was to the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div> Some tone adjustment maybe, but Yu-Shan is not exactly a welcoming place; it's kind of built around the premise of being tremendously elitist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:10:36-07:00","id":654480,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that DBs fill the role really well. They are themselves elitist asshole who are used to being told they're the cream of the crop, when actually they're the weakest of the chosen even at their best and they're now a pale and dilute shadow even of that. They're just begging for a scene where they get their ass kicked by a dawn or watch a Lunar effortlessly defeat the monster that killed the rest of their brotherhood and leading to said DB pounding the ground and saying it's not fair. Then they get to go me home and beat a slave to death to make themselves feel better about their tiny supernatural penis.<br /> <br /> Buuut sometimes it can feel like an endorsement from the game to remind people that DBs are the bitch exalted when it shows up all the time. Like the terrestrial exalted are often presented as scary, but they're less scary because they're badasses and more scary because if you piss them off they'll order your entire neighbourhood to be killed and their heads to be put on pikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:31:13-07:00","id":654493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're just begging for a scene where they get their ass kicked by a dawn or watch a Lunar effortlessly defeat the monster that killed the rest of their brotherhood and leading to said DB pounding the ground and saying it's not fair. Then they get to go me home and beat a slave to death to make themselves feel better about their tiny supernatural penis.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that's just swell. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like the terrestrial exalted are often presented as scary, but they're less scary because they're badasses and more scary because if you piss them off they'll order your entire neighbourhood to be killed and their heads to be put on pikes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even if this premise was true, which I don't quite hold with... so? It would be weird to play a character within the setting who would be so detached and faux-jaded as to look upon their burning homestead and scoff &quot;oh sure, you've got the iron fist of the Empire, but you can't have sword fights leaping around with elaborate computer effects, so psshaaw&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:04:39-07:00","id":654526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654493#post654493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that's just swell. </div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zl_HfTZ69Xw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zl_HfTZ69Xw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zl_HfTZ69Xw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zl_HfTZ69Xw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's a super common trope to have the snooty dude who thinks he's better than everyone else because he's had the best training and the best blood in the empire...and then ending up with his face in the dirt after fighting one of the backwater mongrels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654493#post654493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even if this premise was true, which I don't quite hold with... so? It would be weird to play a character within the setting who would be so detached and faux-jaded as to look upon their burning homestead and scoff &amp;quot;oh sure, you've got the iron fist of the Empire, but you can't have sword fights leaping around with elaborate computer effects, so psshaaw&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're a celestial exalt that wouldn't really happen, is my point. If you're a dirt farming peasant or an overworked lumberjack or something because they'll burn your whole family alive for shit that isn't even your fault. What's frightening isn't their power is their ruthlessness. If you can't take a sword and slay 100 men with it, then every day you might be risking death.<br /> <br /> It can sort of feel like the DBs are a schoolyard bully, but the celestial exalted are six foot two bikers. In the schoolyard the bully and their posse are scary little assholes. But in the grand scheme of things that little twerp can't really play with the big boys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:16:35-07:00","id":654528,"title":"","content":"If ex three does as promised and makes mortals matter more, that'd help a ton, in all the games I've ever played as a Solar I have never been afraid of the legions or really even the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:18:49-07:00","id":654531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654480#post654480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't help that DBs fill the role really well. They are themselves elitist asshole who are used to being told they're the cream of the crop, when actually they're the weakest of the chosen even at their best and they're now a pale and dilute shadow even of that. They're just begging for a scene where they get their ass kicked by a dawn or watch a Lunar effortlessly defeat the monster that killed the rest of their brotherhood and leading to said DB pounding the ground and saying it's not fair. Then they get to go me home and beat a slave to death to make themselves feel better about their tiny supernatural penis.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654526#post654526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can sort of feel like the DBs are a schoolyard bully, but the celestial exalted are six foot two bikers. In the schoolyard the bully and their posse are scary little assholes. But in the grand scheme of things that little twerp can't really play with the big boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little confused. Are you positing that this is somehow desirable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:32:32-07:00","id":654538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654531#post654531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm a little confused. Are you positing that this is somehow desirable?</div> </div> </div> </div>KIND of. In some ways it's just a classic theme that leads to the I am Prince Vegeta/I am a god/I am a centurion scene, which leads to them getting smashed in the face by Broly, cut open by Leonidas's spear and shanked in the chest by the Celtic she-wolf warrior.<br /> <br /> But if taken too far it can start to feel like the DBs and their legions are only there to soften up the enemy Abyssals army for your assault. (No joke I've seen DB legions used in this way three times more often than I've seen them be the actual threat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:40:11-07:00","id":654565,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand this part of the topic made me look back through an RPG.Net thread that I recalled as having been more interesting and thoughtful, when it really... wasn't. I don't blame you, thread... I don't blame you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:48:59-07:00","id":654573,"title":"","content":"Okay like, Kill La Kill right? Satsuki is the high breeding scion of the life fiber fashion empire thing right? Trying not to spoil too much here. Ryuko is a crass, uncultured girl who I think is technically homeless before Mako takes her in. She rises up and kicks Satsuki to the curb because she's the badass heroine and Satauki in spite of all her allies, all her planning, all her training all her family connections, just can't beat her. So that's the good part, the classic tearing down of the elite.<br /> <br /> So now imagine that instead, her mother was the real final boss and she was so far above her daughter that the two couldn't even complete, like it wasn't even close. Ryuko can do it though, she can even beat her if she tries hard enough. Satsuki on the other hand is now relegated to background character, she can't even contribute to help either side because theyre so far above her that anything she'd do would just get in the way. I've also run into exactly this, in fact in the last second Ed game I ever played, where we had to leave all our DB allies at home because the only thing they could possibly add to the charge into Malfeas would be to die and push one of the celestial exalts into heroic effort mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:12:20-07:00","id":654584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a super common trope to have the snooty dude who thinks he's better than everyone else because he's had the best training and the best blood in the empire...and then ending up with his face in the dirt after fighting one of the backwater mongrels.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am aware. It is actually an aspect of the Solar narrative that holds a special place for me. I just find the idea of projecting it onto the Dragon Blooded with a kind of giddy anticipation to be kind of offputting, It reminds me of when people criticised Return of the Scarlet Empress with their own alternative fates for her, and it's like... chaining her ghost to provide eternal lamentations of her own failings as a permanent warning against excessive ambition is certainly fitting to the setting, but could you breathe a bit less heavily when talking about it, person? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you're a celestial exalt that wouldn't really happen, is my point.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your point is faulty. While you're slaying a hundred soldiers, ten people are walking around the fight to set your family on fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:38:36-07:00","id":654594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654538#post654538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KIND of. In some ways it's just a classic theme that leads to the I am Prince Vegeta/I am a god/I am a centurion scene, which leads to them getting smashed in the face by Broly, cut open by Leonidas's spear and shanked in the chest by the Celtic she-wolf warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all well and good for a purely non-interactive narrative but then when you turn around and make Worfing a normalized touchstone for an entire playable splat, I think that's really problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:02:20-07:00","id":654663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654058#post654058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Property? What?<br /> That can't be true. Even Dragon Kings have more rights in Heaven than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it's quite THAT bad, but in Heaven, killing a Terrestrial is basically a minor misdemeanor. Severity 2, I believe.<br /> <br /> You can literally get in more trouble for attacking said DB's would be killer. Which is pretty damned fucked up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:36:48-07:00","id":654673,"title":"","content":"It's also really hot and humid here so I'm sorry if I sound like more of a dick than normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T20:55:36-07:00","id":654732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654429#post654429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some tone adjustment maybe, but Yu-Shan is not exactly a welcoming place; it's kind of built around the premise of being tremendously elitist.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the gameline continues to suggest that the gods look down on and sneer at the Exalted, or that Exalted are considered property in Yu-Shan, or pretty much any of the bullshit 2nd edition said, I will be very disappointed. I just don't think that having an entire, major world and setting in Exalted, populaed by people who look down their noses on the Exalted and consider them, not just lesser beings, but insignificant, unimportant and, barely even sentient, and then have those guys running reality, is good for the gameline.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the gods (like everyone else in the setting) should view Exaltation with awe, respect and terror. Not view Exalted as slighty-smarter monkeys.<br /> <br /> The problem with Yu-Shan in 2nd edition is that it made it clear that there were two tiers of Exaltation. The &quot;real&quot; Exalted (Solars, Sidereal and Lunars) whom the gods were scared of, respected and treated as equals, and the &quot;shit-tier&quot; Exalted, the Terrestrials, who were, at best, objects of scorn.<br /> <br /> That was some serious garbage, and I'll be quite disappointed if that concept in any way returns in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T21:43:49-07:00","id":654738,"title":"","content":"I like the Arrogant Gods of Yu-Shan, but there are plenty of ways to portray that than &quot;Exalts of this type are the scum of the earth.&quot; For example, a newly Exalted Solar (or Dragonblooded) might not know all the rituals and procedures of Yu-Shan. Thus the Celestial gods can look down on the Age of Sorrows Exalts because of their poor manners instead of their Exalted status.<br /> <br /> Sort of a &quot;These Dragonblooded don't even know the Hymn of the Unconquered Sun! And that new incarnation of Mera? She put her elbows on the table! What are they teaching down in Creation these days?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-07-2015, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T21:57:41-07:00","id":654742,"title":"","content":"Even then, an Exaltation should still carry a certain level of weight, and I don't think it's good if the game's default assumption is that the gods of Yu-Shan will be jeering and sniggering at your character should your ST choose to take the game to Yu-Shan. <br /> <br /> The Exaltation is the most holy of miracles, and there should be a sense that the gods, who owe their lives and existences to the Exalted, should have some level of respect for the Exalted. And setting it up so that the gods of Yu-Shan consider the Exalted to be goobers until proven otherwise is just not something I can get behind.<br /> <br /> Even the most baseborn Exalt with no training or courtly manners is still one of the Exalted, one of the highest of beings and lords of existence.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't expect that you can go to Yu-Shan and have gods kneel for you, but you also shouldn't assume that they will be looking down their noses at you. In general, I think that the gods should hold a certain respect and reverence for the Exalted, such that they tend to treat them as equals rather than as lesser beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T02:17:52-07:00","id":654905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654742#post654742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, an Exaltation should still carry a certain level of weight, and I don't think it's good if the game's default assumption is that the gods of Yu-Shan will be jeering and sniggering at your character should your ST choose to take the game to Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> The Exaltation is the most holy of miracles, and there should be a sense that the gods, who owe their lives and existences to the Exalted, should have some level of respect for the Exalted. And setting it up so that the gods of Yu-Shan consider the Exalted to be goobers until proven otherwise is just not something I can get behind.<br /> <br /> Even the most baseborn Exalt with no training or courtly manners is still one of the Exalted, one of the highest of beings and lords of existence.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't expect that you can go to Yu-Shan and have gods kneel for you, but you also shouldn't assume that they will be looking down their noses at you. In general, I think that the gods should hold a certain respect and reverence for the Exalted, such that they tend to treat them as equals rather than as lesser beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>probably the right general attitude, with variances and exceptions all over. this is a complex world with complex issues, and I don't think it can be quite summed up like that.<br /> <br /> for example, the Terrestrial Gods are more likely to have antagonistic relationships with the Dragon-Blooded, while some Celestial Gods are more likely to have antagonistic relationships with the Sidereals. Some gods on the Threshold might be more amenable to the Lunars.<br /> <br /> some gods are more likely to be snobbish than others and hold Exalts to high standards, particularly ones in power, as they expect great things from the person chosen by the greatest of the gods. while those not in power will be friendly to try and get in their good graces. some might be tired or disgruntled with them for being trouble-makers, some might just wish for them to go away so they can get back to something more peaceful and just not say it.....and thats just for the normal four.<br /> <br /> But then you have Abyssals, who kind of murder this general attitude with a soulsteel axe to the face. Because everyone knows that the Underworld is bad news to the gods, so they're very likely to treat the Abyssals very differently from the other four Exalted- its hard for anyone to like a guy whose only purpose is to go around killing things and is Chosen by the souls of your slain enemies, so I'm thinking that the Gods will be far more likely to not treat an Abyssal with any form of respect than a Solar. A Solar is that guy returning from the First Age and holds the potential to make everything great again if he plays his cards right. An Abyssal is a guy coming forth to steal away all your worship and replace it with ghosts and the cults worshipping them while killing the entire land around them into darkness.<br /> <br /> and of course, there is Liminals, who seem to be fighting against Abyssals, so probably respected if known at all.<br /> <br /> Infernals would just be outright hated because their powers are reminiscent of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> Exigents are of course made from one of the many smaller gods so....they are probably respected, but is subject to varying circumstances as with all things Exigent.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are just plain foreign, but I doubt the gods would like the way they treat gods, as Autochthon organized them differently in Autochthonia.<br /> <br /> finally, Getimians are made to fight against fate and the Sidereals. this can also be a varying thing, as one hand, they are fighting against fate and the gods could hate them for that, on the other hand they're fighting against Sidereals and could love them for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T02:24:23-07:00","id":654910,"title":"","content":"Even with Abyssals, Infernals and other Exalted who are &quot;unnatural&quot;, the general attitude of gods in Yu-Shan should be outright terror and fear rather than being viewed with mockery and subject to jeers. <br /> <br /> I just don't think that it's good if <i>any</i> Exalted-type is generally viewed with disdain. If an Exalt proves himself to be totally incompetent, then sure, the gods and everyone else can look down on him as pathetic. But that shouldn't be the basic, initial attitude from a vast part of the setting towards an entire splat of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T03:31:38-07:00","id":654962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654732#post654732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the gameline continues to suggest that the gods look down on and sneer at the Exalted, or that Exalted are considered property in Yu-Shan, or pretty much any of the bullshit 2nd edition said, I will be very disappointed. I just don't think that having an entire, major world and setting in Exalted, populaed by people who look down their noses on the Exalted and consider them, not just lesser beings, but insignificant, unimportant and, barely even sentient, and then have those guys running reality, is good for the gameline.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the gods (like everyone else in the setting) should view Exaltation with awe, respect and terror. Not view Exalted as slighty-smarter monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excluded middle plus pretty ridiculous exaggeration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Yu-Shan in 2nd edition is that it made it clear that there were two tiers of Exaltation. The &quot;real&quot; Exalted (Solars, Sidereal and Lunars) whom the gods were scared of, respected and treated as equals, and the &quot;shit-tier&quot; Exalted, the Terrestrials, who were, at best, objects of scorn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the hyperbole: yes, Compass: Yu-Shan had the line about gods being hardwired to despise Terrestrials because they overthrew the Solars, and generally looked down on them because they can't become Celestial Exalted, which shouldn't be around and arose from a problematic development place.<br /> <br /> The idea that Terrestrials have minimal rights in inhospitable Heaven was in Exalted: the Sidereals. It didn't quite afford much to other Exalted either.<br /> <br /> The statement that the Five Elemental Dragons have power on par with the Incarnae while <i>still</i> being looked down upon as rustic and uncouth by the Celestial gods is in Games of Divinity.<br /> <br /> Think about what that implies about how we're supposed to think of the attitudes of Celestial gods. &quot;Hey, you're explicitly vastly more powerful than me, but you live on a 'lower' strata of the universe, so I'm going to look down my nose at you&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think it makes for a good, strong sense of a distant, elitist, Dunsany and Lee style realm of the gods to have them be so haughty.<br /> <br /> I can see reasons to be hung up on the idea that people aren't automatically deferential towards the character group one would play, but they are uncharitable.<br /> <br /> Heh, it reminds me of my ideas of a scene in which some antagonist (or even caustic mentor figure) makes the typical speech of a player's character being weak, and that player becoming really indignant and pointing to all of the things on their character sheet that empirically demonstrate that their character is not weak.<br /> <br /> I mean, by and large, nobody should be viewing &quot;Exaltation&quot; as <i>anything</i>, or at least not as something that overrides the actual character around it. This is part of why I disdain this excessive scrutiny of the concept of an Exaltation in the first place (without losing the image of a divine fire that anoints you from on high). No, the Exalted should not be looked on as slightly-smarter monkeys (I mean, nobody ever said that they should, so perhaps dial it back a bit), at the same time that they should not be looking at them as meat puppets for the impressive magic superweapon.<br /> <br /> When you're focusing on them as characters who have backgrounds and perform actions, you can have other people look on them in less than stellar terms, either as a reflection of prejudice or a halfway rational assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T05:20:55-07:00","id":655035,"title":"","content":"I feel like Exaltation should be kinda like a doctorate, or a knighthood. Would you tell a doctor or a knight that their title is meaningless because of how they got it? Probably not - more likely, your default assumption wiuld be that you are looking at a Very Accomplished Person. Maybe they will disappoint you later, but if all you know about them at first is that they are entitled then your first response is probably deferrence, not contempt.<br /> <br /> Alternately, Exaltation is like visibly carrying a firearm. Bearing a gun automatically makes you dangerous, someone to watch - people who do not already trust you or are not similarly armed will avoid you. Being Chosn't isn't just a character trait - it's a visible power that grants mortals the ability to do godly feats. The gods of Yu-Shan should know better than anyone that the Chosen can kill the divine and reshape the world at their whim.<br /> <br /> Having the gods in heaven be snooty is fine in theory... but the Dragonblooded aren't a good target for their attitude. The very existence of the Immaculate religion proves that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:26:13-07:00","id":655091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they will disappoint you later, but if all you know about them at first is that they are entitled then your first response is probably deferrence, not contempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are a sizeable number of people who are contemptuous of the person or concept of doctors as a general thing, for reasons that range from forms of anti-intellectualism to disdain for real or imagined elitism.<br /> <br /> I mean, if one has a reason to be contemptuous of a particular doctor, it's not much of a stretch to assume that the same qualities go for all doctors.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about modern knights, that's even easier; it's super easy to look at the whole persistence of the concept as a weird, self-congratulatory elitist club, or a bizarre need to give accomplished people some extra little thing to project that they're accomplished.<br /> <br /> If all doctors went around wearing a big golden crown as a little gift to themselves to show off their being doctors, would you treat that with deference?<br /> <br /> I can't really think of any category of people that has not been looked on with contempt by at least one other category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very existence of the Immaculate religion proves that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Philosophy is mostly pointed at Terrestrial gods; it holds force with Heaven almost solely because the Sidereals advocate for it.<br /> <br /> Sure, at least part of why they're able to do so is because Dragon Blooded hegemony provides a means to inflict damage on their worshippers, but that doesn't strictly imply lack of contempt for the Dragon Blooded; rather the opposite, really.<br /> <br /> Or does one think that nobody ever held violent criminals or dictatorial regimes in contempt?<br /> <br /> Hence my comparison on Hindu vardas. Although right now, I'm also thinking of something like the pre-war Deep South; whatever the uses of the overseers, they have no place in the Big House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:50:29-07:00","id":655115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=654910#post654910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't think that it's good if <i>any</i> Exalted-type is generally viewed with disdain. If an Exalt proves himself to be totally incompetent, then sure, the gods and everyone else can look down on him as pathetic. But that shouldn't be the basic, initial attitude from a vast part of the setting towards an entire splat of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not advocating that gods look down on Exalts because they are Exalts of a particular type. Rather Creation has fallen since the First Age and those who were raised in the Age of Sorrows are uncultured to the Celestial Gods. Hell, a Well-Spoken Seventh Legion Dragonblood might impress the Celestial gods more than a mud behind their ears Solar.<br /> <br /> Not all Celestial gods will think the same way. One might want to pull a &quot;My Fair Lady&quot; on the poor Solar. Another might see beyond the Solar's bad table manners and understand why the Unconquered Sun choose this person and offer support to their endeavors. Yet another god might eventually be won over by the Solar (got to use those social charms for something!). God should have their own opinions and not be pre-programmed by some Creation-Ruling Mandate.<br /> <br /> To summarize, I like the &quot;Most Celestial Gods think Creation is dirty and look down on those who are raised there&quot;, but can do without &quot;All Celestial Gods think Dragonblood are the Scum of the Earth.&quot; You can have the Celestial God Arrogance without the Terrestrial Prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T08:10:29-07:00","id":655166,"title":"","content":"The existence of prejudice isn\u2019t the problem so much as ubiquitous and insurmountable prejudice from people who'll probably call for an army of Celestial Lions if you cause a fuss.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T08:45:23-07:00","id":655189,"title":"","content":"I have only skimmed the Games of Divinity section but I think it does a pretty good job.<br /> <br /> How I prefer to see it is that Celestial gods look down on the Terrestrial sphere and everything in it, so they do generally consider themselves better than everything from there, even Dragon-Blooded and the Five Elemental Dragons. Terrestrial gods are more likely to fear and resent Dragon-Blooded, and especially Immaculates. After the Great Contagion, many gods in both worlds view the Dragon-Blooded as too weak to defend Creation. But most also respect/fear their power and ability to kill gods Dead, and don't view them as non-people.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, most gods view Solars with some mix of fear and respect, possibly mixed with hope, awe, and/or terror. Solars have the potential to upset the whole status quo, to return things to the laws of Heaven, or who knows what! They used to rule the world and they might do so again. That's super scary if you like your corruption and really great if you want to restore the law. On the other hand some say their return will destroy the world! You want to be careful about pissing them off. That doesn't mean that most gods are inclined to defer to them purely on principle, not when they rarely defer to each other when they don't have to. If you're careful and good at manipulation, an ignorant Solar or Lunar can become a valuable tool as well as (or maybe instead of) a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T09:01:32-07:00","id":655197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/649014-why-would-a-db-of-the-realm-join-a-group-of-anathema?p=655189#post655189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I prefer to see it is that Celestial gods look down on the Terrestrial sphere and everything in it, so they do generally consider themselves better than everything from there, even Dragon-Blooded and the Five Elemental Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Five Elemental Dragons are the children of Gaia, and more powerful than any gods but the Incarnae. So I don't think that'd be a healthy attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T09:26:47-07:00","id":655204,"title":"","content":"Prejudice is often foolish. Lots of people are stupid, and stupidly prejudiced.<br /> Anyway, I think they <i><b>also</b></i> fear and respect them. And are pretty sure they're all safely asleep or never leave the Poles. It's complicated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-07-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T13:19:02-07:00","id":1405191,"title":"","content":"Wow, I actually found this old as HELL topic of mine from years back. I know necrobumping is generally bad juju on forums, but with my recent renewed interest in Exalted I've still been working on this goofy as hell story and have actually come up with reasons for why the three DB's that follow our Eclipse hero--Kairos--do so.<br /> <br /> Firstly, Cathak Vadara. A Fire-Aspect, he is almost worryingly emotionless to the point where he just follow Kairos because why not. He's so utterly uninvested in the whole Immaculate Philosophy that he sees no reason not to examine one of the Anathema for himself. Besides, Kairos was a scion of house Ledaal. No Ledaal would just <i>let </i>a demon in them.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Nellens Suguha. Suguha was born of two unexalted parents and viewed as useless from the very moment she was born--put through the primary and secondary schools only because <i>all</i> dynasts were. There was zero hope for her to exalt, and her family and fellow dynasts treated her like absolute garbage. She ended up making friends with Kairos (who was born to DB parents and had like Breeding 5 by 2e standards) However, she ended up Exalting into a Water-Aspect at like age <i>11</i>, when some dynasts and patrician bullies threw Kairos into a lake and Suguha desperately jumped in after him. Her social status improved instantly, but it actually had the opposite effect on her than her peers hoped--seeing the same people who viewed her as worthless trash suddenly suck up to her or even just treat her as some social equal and actively denying the endless bullying they had put her through showed her that the Dynast was a bitter brutal place where one's worth could arbitraily change on a whim. When Kairos exalted into a Eclipse, she decided to hang on, already disillusioned with the realm.<br /> <br /> Finally, Maris. Hoo boy. Kurasi was born to a peasant woman on the east coasts of the Blessed Isle, living her whole life in constant starvation and poverty. She attended the teachings of the Immaculate Order, but they only filled her heart with bitter hatred for it. The texts told her that she was suffering because of a past life she had no knowledge from--that she and her mother were paying penance for things they had never done, that they <i>deserved</i> to live nothing but bitter hard lives of endless pain. The only grace the Order told her was that if she worked hard, she might bless her next incarnation to be a bit better. But that was no help to <i>her</i>, and with zero memories of her supposed former lives, why should she believe the monks? And how could she do that anyway, trapped in an endless cycle of poverty? The things the monks said only made sense to those whose lives weren't endless struggle. For someone like her, they provided nothing.<br /> <br /> When she was 15, she begged some dynasts for food, having not eaten for three whole days. They mocked her, telling her that she should make way for Princes of the Earth. She asked them if their coffers were so tight that they could not spare to feed a <i>single</i> child. One child. The dynasts threw around jade like it was candy and here they could not lift a finger to help her. When one went to punch her for her insolence, she took the hit head on and exalted into an Earth-Aspect right there. Quickly, they apologized and arranged for her to be given typical Outcaste education. Like Suguha (but much worse) the fact that random chance led them to no longer treat her like detritus absolutely snuffed whatever minor spark of faith she still had. Fuck the Realm. Fuck the Order. Fuck all of this. When the only friend she had during her year of education exalted into a Lunar Anathema and was brutally slaughtered for it, and her own mother died in the street despite Maris begging the realm to at least give her <i>something, </i>the very firewood said faith once burned upon was vaporized into ash. She ran away and escaped on a ship to the Threshold. She met Kairos there.<br /> <br /> Notably, Maris thinks that Kairos is a demon still. She just hates the Realm <i>so godsdamn much</i> that she'd rather throw her follow a demon than it--and besides, these supposed demons can't be anywhere near as bad as the Realm, right?<br /> <br /> So there we have it. One dude is just a borderline sociopath who only follows whatever will lead him to the truth of the world, one girl is a friend of our Solar and disillusioned with the Realm, one girl just absolutely <i>despises</i> it.<br /> <br /> Wow, you can really tell these characters were made in order because they become better written with each one lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}